invariant: INV-26
file: quic_aes_soft.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh quic_aes
reason: the key expansion's loop in quic_aes_soft.c runs one word past
  round_keys, so the
  last four stores land outside the aes_key_schedule and inside whatever
  the caller placed after it, which under TRANSPORT=quic is the rest of
  ch_quic. INV-26 is what admits a table-driven AES into this tree, and
  quic_aes_harness is what holds the admitted code to memory safety at
  its real bound, so this is the bug that harness exists to catch.
  docs/proofs.md requires planting it once and landing it. Each run is a
  proof of seconds, but the catch line names proof/prove-one.sh, so this
  belongs to the nightly's test-invariants-proof-backed job.

--- old
    for (size_t i = AES_128_KEY; i < (size_t)AES_ROUND_KEYS * AES_BLOCK; i += 4) {
--- new
    for (size_t i = AES_128_KEY; i <= (size_t)AES_ROUND_KEYS * AES_BLOCK; i += 4) {
